7b. ASSEMBLER PROBE — the receipt tested against the REAL ledger tool
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
I did not run ledger-assemble against the repository (it writes
i18n/ledger.json and i18n/receipts/). Instead I built a scratch tree holding
byte copies of the six catalogue files and ran the real assembler with --repo
pointed at it, so the tool's own validation ran on my receipt with no repo
write:

  SC="$LOCAL_OPERATOR_SCRATCHPAD"; R="$SC/assemble-probe/repo"
  mkdir -p "$R/src/i18n/catalogues/en" "$R/src/i18n/catalogues/ru"
  cp <worktree>/src/i18n/catalogues/{en,ru}/<ns>.json into the same paths
  node <worktree>/scripts/i18n/ledger-assemble.mjs --repo "$R" --locale ru \
    --file src/i18n/catalogues/ru/<ns>.json \
    --auditor-instance bcfbdd468d00 --auditor-model deepseek/deepseek-flash \
    --result <clean|clean|clean-with-findings> --date 2026-11-10 \
    --translator-agent i18n-translator \
    --translator-model anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5 \
    --note "passed; evidence i18n/audits/evidence/ru/<ns>/bcfbdd468d00/record.json" \
    --receipt "$SC/ru-ds-bcfbdd468d00.json"

